792
00:33:26,760 --> 00:33:29,010
So how do we balance the two, right?

793
00:33:29,010 --> 00:33:31,410
How do we instill in students

794
00:33:31,410 --> 00:33:33,720
a desire to submit original work,

795
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:36,240
use AI in responsible ways,

796
00:33:36,240 --> 00:33:41,067
and still think about the curriculum enrichment

797
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:46,069
where my AI skills might be embedded in some of the courses

798
00:33:46,069 --> 00:33:47,700
and things like that.

799
00:33:47,700 --> 00:33:49,920
So, I'm going to pose...

800
00:33:49,920 --> 00:33:53,313
It's a really simple question for my panel here.

801
00:33:54,360 --> 00:33:55,620
Andrea, you wanna start us off?

802
00:33:55,620 --> 00:33:56,453
- Sure.

803
00:33:59,910 --> 00:34:02,070
What we've been talking about at Skyline College

804
00:34:02,070 --> 00:34:04,950
is working with it, rather than against it,

805
00:34:04,950 --> 00:34:07,290
and finding ways to have the students

806
00:34:07,290 --> 00:34:10,680
engage in critical thinking and evaluating AI content,

807
00:34:10,680 --> 00:34:14,220
rather than just wholesale have ChatGPT write your essay.

808
00:34:14,220 --> 00:34:17,010
It's very difficult to AI-proof,

809
00:34:17,010 --> 00:34:19,230
which I've had this conversation many times,

810
00:34:19,230 --> 00:34:22,260
those detector tools are not that accurate.

811
00:34:22,260 --> 00:34:24,180
But how can you find ways to make it authentic

812
00:34:24,180 --> 00:34:25,290
and real with the students?

813
00:34:25,290 --> 00:34:28,350
And involve them in the process.

814
00:34:28,350 --> 00:34:29,793
Involve them in the process.

815
00:34:31,453 --> 00:34:34,080
- I think the number one thing I would highlight

816
00:34:34,080 --> 00:34:35,670
