00:38:58,890 --> 00:39:03,480
And so it's evident, even in how we create our acronyms,

923
00:39:03,480 --> 00:39:06,900
that we want people to be in the driver's seat,

924
00:39:06,900 --> 00:39:09,330
not just in the loop, but in the driver's seat.

925
00:39:09,330 --> 00:39:11,130
And so I'm gonna ask my panel,

926
00:39:11,130 --> 00:39:13,920
and we'll start with Matt this time around:

927
00:39:13,920 --> 00:39:14,820
How do we do that?

928
00:39:15,810 --> 00:39:20,490
- So I took a while to take a look at this question,

929
00:39:20,490 --> 00:39:25,050
but AI extends access.

930
00:39:25,050 --> 00:39:29,103
So, it supports our after-hours questions and answers.

931
00:39:29,940 --> 00:39:31,770
But it doesn't replace us, okay?

932
00:39:31,770 --> 00:39:34,830
It doesn't replace office hours, it extends it,

933
00:39:34,830 --> 00:39:38,280
