00:42:05,460 --> 00:42:07,500
So there's things that humans do best.

992
00:42:07,500 --> 00:42:09,807
There's things that technology does best,

993
00:42:09,807 --> 00:42:11,640
and so we should make sure we identify those.

994
00:42:11,640 --> 00:42:13,920
All of us have probably an example in our life.

995
00:42:13,920 --> 00:42:15,840
If I wanna quickly heat food,

996
00:42:15,840 --> 00:42:18,420
microwave is a great avenue to do that very quickly.

997
00:42:18,420 --> 00:42:19,920
I don't have to start a fire,

998
00:42:19,920 --> 00:42:21,450
I don't have to cook that food.

999
00:42:21,450 --> 00:42:23,250
Technology is better served right there

1000
00:42:23,250 --> 00:42:25,680
because it opens up my human capital time

1001
00:42:25,680 --> 00:42:27,180
to go do something else.

1002
00:42:27,180 --> 00:42:29,190
So, we all have a different example in our life.

1003
00:42:29,190 --> 00:42:30,720
So think through that.

1004
00:42:30,720 --> 00:42:32,644
Embrace technology where it is at its best

1005
00:42:32,644 --> 00:42:34,950
to open you up to do the other things.

1006
00:42:34,950 --> 00:42:37,020
So in terms of teaching and learning,

1007
00:42:37,020 --> 00:42:38,610
figure out what takes you away,

1008
00:42:38,610 --> 00:42:40,920
and I think both of them just did exactly that.

